<Doc>
    <Code code={`abide scaffold ledger
cd ledger
abide dev`} />

    <Section title="What it writes">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>src/page.abide</code></td><td>the page at <code>/</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>src/layout.abide</code></td><td>the root layout: the document its pages are served in, and the <code>&lt;script server&gt;</code> holding the lifecycle hooks</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>package.json</code>, <code>tsconfig.json</code>, <code>biome.json</code></td><td>the toolchain, configured</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p><code>#src/*</code> is the one import alias, mapping onto <code>src/</code>. Grow the app
        by subject — a <code>src/billing/</code> with its own pages, components and
        <code>server</code> — and its pages answer below <code>/billing</code>, with no file moved
        to make room.</p>

        <p>Nothing generated is a framework file you are asked not to edit. The layout is a real
        component writing a real HTML document, and the page is a component too.</p>

        <p>Read on: <a href={url('/reference/configuration')}>Configuration</a> ·
        <a href={url('/pages/give-pages-the-same-chrome')}>Layouts</a></p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`abide` with no command prints usage">
        <p><code>abide</code>, <code>abide -h</code> and <code>abide --help</code> all print usage
        <strong>generated from the command list</strong>. It is generated rather than written, so a
        command that exists is a command the help mentions and there is no second place for one to
        go missing.</p>

        <p>Read on: <a href={url('/reference/cli')}>CLI</a></p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Where to go from the scaffold">
        <p>The scaffolded page holds a reactive value and shows it. That is the whole of the first
        thing to learn — a value, and markup that follows it — and everything else on this site is a
        name for something you will want once that is boring.</p>

        <p>Read on: <a href={url('/start/your-first-page')}>First page</a> ·
        <a href={url('/start/what-abide-is-for')}>Why abide</a></p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Next">
        <ul>
            <li><a href={url('/ship/run-the-app-while-you-work')}>Dev server</a> — what <code>abide
            dev</code> does while you work</li>
            <li><a href={url('/start/your-first-page')}>First page</a> — the walk-through from
            here</li>
            <li><a href={url('/reference/cli')}>CLI</a> — every command and flag</li>
        </ul>
    </Section>
</Doc>
